    "body": "Fair point. I think only a subset of those are the sort of \"read-only zero\" where it \"is read-only and reads as 0\". A lot of them are *always* read-only zero, e.g.\r\n\r\n> medeleg[11] is read-only zero\r\n\r\n> Bits of mie that are not writable must be read-only zero.\r\n\r\nI think it *is* subtle and somewhat confusing and probably could be improved (maybe hyperlink them to the CSR modulation section and add an explanation of what exactly it means?). Probably something for another PR.\r\n\r\nIn this PR I think we should at least use the same wording for both `menvcfg.SSE` and `henvcfg.SSE` though. Should I change the `henvcfg.SSE` one to `read-only zero` instead?",
